<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 198,100 running bales (RB) were 95 percent higher than the previous week and one-fifth above the 4-week average.  The major buyers were Indonesia (40,500 RB), China (39,900 RB), South Korea (35,500 RB), Japan (29,200 RB), and Hong Kong (14,300 RB).  Reductions were reported for unknown destinations (4,600 RB).</p>
<p>Exports of 69,800 RB were off 27 percent from the week earlier, but exceeded the 4-week average by 36 percent.  Asian destinations accounted for 65 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 29 percent; and West European, 6 percent.</p>
</text>
